SUMMARY: Fall Walk: Finch Recreational Trail & Park Adventure! 🌾🚶‍
 ♂️ (16KM) 
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🍁 Fall Walk: Finch Recreation
 al Trail & Park Adventure! 🌾\n\n### An Easy\, Flat Fall Walk Through To
 ronto's Green Spaces\n\nLooking for an easy way to enjoy the fall colours 
 without tackling a difficult hike?\nJoin us for a relaxed walk from **Pion
 eer Village Station to Finch Station**\, travelling through Black Creek Pa
 rkland and along the **Finch Recreational Trail**.\n\nThis is one of our m
 embers' favourite walks for a reason. The route is mostly flat and takes u
 s through open fields\, wooded areas\, and quiet green spaces that feel su
 rprisingly far removed from the city.\n\nWe'll take our time\, enjoy the c
 hanging leaves\, stop for a break by **Dufferin Creek**\, and spend the da
 y walking and getting to know each other.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our
  **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018
 gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 🚶‍♂️ What We'll Do\n\nWe'll start outsi
 de **Pioneer Village Station** and make our way through Black Creek Parkla
 nd before joining the Finch Recreational Trail.\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n*
  Walk through Black Creek Parkland 🌳\n* Follow the Finch Recreational T
 rail\n* Enjoy the fall colours and changing scenery 🍂\n* Stop for a bre
 ak near Dufferin Creek\n* Have some time for conversation and photos\n* Co
 ntinue along the trail toward Finch Station\n\nThis is a **long but easy\,
  mostly flat walk**. There are no major hills or difficult terrain\, but y
 ou'll want comfortable shoes and enough energy for the full route.\n\n***\
 n\n## 🍂 Fall Is the Best Time to Do This Walk\n\nThere's something part
 icularly nice about this trail in the fall. The air is cooler\, the leaves
  are changing\, and the open stretches of the trail give you plenty of roo
 m to slow down and enjoy the season.\nIt's a good walk if you want to get 
 outside without feeling like you're climbing a mountain.\nAnd as always\, 
 **the activity is the container. The people you meet along the way are the
  real experience.**\n\n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Loca
 tion:** Outside Pioneer Village Station\, at the corner of Steeles Avenue 
 West and Northwest Gate (East Side)\, in front of the York University sign
 .\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **Meetup Time:** 11:00 AM sh
 arp\nI will only wait **5 minutes**.\n**Early is on time. On time is late.
 **\n🏁 **End Point:** Finch Station\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n*
 *$5 cash in person or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\nTh
 is fee helps support the group and allows us to continue organizing events
  throughout Toronto.\n\n***\n\n## 🎒 What to Bring\n\n💧 Water\n👟 C
 omfortable walking shoes\n🥪 A snack or light lunch\n🧥 A fall jacket 
 or sweater\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis walk is great for:\n
 \n* Anyone who enjoys fall scenery\n* People looking for an easy\, flat tr
 ail\n* Anyone who wants to get back into walking\n* People who enjoy explo
 ring Toronto's green spaces\n* Anyone looking for a relaxed social outing\
 n* People who want to meet new people while getting some fresh air\n\nYou'
 re welcome to RSVP ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsu
 re about your schedule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be
  cancelled or changed\, so please keep an eye on the event page for update
 s.\n\n👤 **Organizer: Mathew**\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or ema
 il **torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**.\n\n**Come for the fall colours
 .**\n**Stay for the friendship.** 🍁💛
