SUMMARY:GHOST TOUR - 👻 The Ghosts of University of Toronto 🎃 with Di
 nner!
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n# 🎃 The Ghosts of the Universit
 y of Toronto 👻\n\n### A 90-Minute Halloween Ghost Walk Through Toronto'
 s Haunted History\n\nL\nooking for something a little different this Hallo
 ween season?\n\nJoin us for a **guided ghost walk through the University o
 f Toronto campus and its eerie surroundings**\, exploring some of the stor
 ies\, legends\, and strange histories hidden in one of Toronto's oldest ne
 ighbourhoods.\nThis isn't one of our regular walks where we're simply foll
 owing a trail and enjoying the scenery.\n\n**This is a curated storytellin
 g experience.**\n\nI've researched the locations\, developed the route\, a
 nd put together the stories specifically for this experience. We'll explor
 e some of the darker corners of the university and surrounding neighbourho
 ods while uncovering the people\, places\, and legends that have given the
 m their haunted reputations.\n\n🕯️ Along the way\, we'll hear stories
  about:\n\n* What the Christies — yes\, *Mr. Christie Cookies* — were 
 hiding in their mansion 🍪\n* The restless little girl who is never happ
 y 👧\n* What might really be lurking inside Queen's Park 👀\n* Haunted
  stories connected to University of Toronto buildings\n* The Royal Conserv
 atory of Music\n* The Royal Ontario Museum\n* And some other stories that 
 are better experienced after dark... 👻\n\nYou don't have to believe in 
 ghosts.\nYou just have to enjoy a good story.\n\n📱 Don't forget to join
  our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsA
 i018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n## 👻 What We'll Do\n\nWe'll spend approximat
 ely **90 minutes walking through the University of Toronto campus and surr
 ounding streets**\, stopping at locations connected to Toronto's haunted h
 istory.\n\nAlong the way we'll:\n\n* Hear stories about some of Toronto's 
 most intriguing characters and locations\n* Explore the darker history of 
 the University of Toronto\n* Visit locations associated with ghost stories
  and local legends\n* Learn the history behind some of the buildings aroun
 d us\n* Walk through Queen's Park and the surrounding area\n* Finish at th
 e **Royal Ontario Museum**\n\nWe'll remain **outside the buildings** throu
 ghout the experience.\nThe walking pace will be moderate\, with plenty of 
 stops along the way for stories.\n\n***\n\n## 🕯️ This Is More Than a 
 Walk\n\nOur regular walks are about getting outside\, exploring Toronto\, 
 and meeting people.\nThis one is different.\n\n**This is a guided storytel
 ling experience.**\n\nThe route and stories have been researched and devel
 oped specifically for this event\, so you're not just following me from on
 e location to another — you're getting a story about the city as we go.\
 nAnd because it's Halloween season\, we'll be doing it after dark. 🎃\n\
 n***\n\n## 🍂 What to Expect\n\nThis is an outdoor walking experience\, 
 so please dress appropriately for the weather.\nWe'll be walking for appro
 ximately **90 minutes**\, with regular stops for storytelling.\n\nThere is
  **no entry into any buildings**\, so you won't need to worry about museum
  admission or other entrance fees.\nAnd while some of the stories are genu
 inely creepy\, this isn't designed to be a horror attraction.\n\nIt's **To
 ronto history\, local legends\, and storytelling with a spooky twist.**\n\
 n***\n\n## 🧢 Meetup Details\n\n📍 **Meeting Location:** In front of t
 he building by the stairs\n🫎 **Look for me in my Moose Hat!**\n⏰ **St
 art Time:** 7:00 PM sharp\nI will only wait **5 minutes.**\n**Early is on 
 time. On time is late.**\n🚶‍♂️ **Walking Pace:** Moderate\n🏁 *
 *End Point:** Royal Ontario Museum\n\n***\n\n## 🎟️ Meetup Fee\n\n**$1
 0 cash or e-transfer**\n📧 **mathewmaclean@hotmail.com**\n\nThis is a **
 curated\, guided storytelling experience**\, rather than one of our regula
 r group walks. The route\, stories\, and history have been researched and 
 developed specifically for this experience.\n\nFood and drinks afterward a
 re optional and are **not included** in the Meetup fee.\n\n***\n\n## 🍻 
 After the Ghost Walk\n\nWe'll finish at the **Royal Ontario Museum**.\n\nF
 or anyone who wants to keep the evening going\, we'll walk about 10 minute
 s over to the **Duke of York** for food\, drinks\, and conversation.\n\nYo
 u don't have to come — but everyone is welcome.\nBecause sometimes the b
 est part of a ghost story is having someone to talk about it with afterwar
 d. 👻\n\n***\n\n## 🌈 Who Is This For?\n\nThis is great for:\n\n* Anyo
 ne who loves ghost stories 👻\n* History buffs\n* People curious about T
 oronto's darker side\n* Fans of Halloween\n* Anyone who enjoys storytellin
 g\n* People looking for something different to do in the city\n* Anyone wh
 o wants to meet new people while exploring Toronto\n\nYou don't need to be
 lieve in ghosts.\n**Just bring your curiosity.**\n\nYou're welcome to RSVP
  ahead of time or just show up on the day if you're unsure about your sche
 dule.\nSometimes things happen and events may need to be cancelled or chan
 ged\, so please keep an eye on the event page for updates.\n👤 **Organiz
 er: Mathew**\n\nQuestions? Post on the event wall or email:\n📧 **toront
 omoviesandoutings@hotmail.com**\n\n**Come for the ghosts. 👻**\n**Stay f
 or the stories.**\n**Leave with a new connection — and maybe a new frien
 d.** 🖤
