SUMMARY:🍁 The Fall Colours of Brickworks (Thanksgiving Walk) 🍂
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\n🍁 **The Fall Colours of Brickwo
 rks (Thanksgiving Walk)** 🍂\n\nCelebrate Thanksgiving with a scenic fal
 l walk through Toronto’s ravines as we make our way to **Evergreen Brick
  Works**. Along the way\, enjoy the crisp autumn air\, brilliant fall colo
 urs\, and a peaceful escape from the city.\n\nWe’ll spend about **30 min
 utes exploring the Brick Works**\, taking in its history\, trails\, and un
 ique setting before heading back through **Mount Pleasant Cemetery** — o
 ne of Toronto’s largest and oldest cemeteries\, with plenty of history a
 nd beautiful seasonal scenery.\nFor those who’d like to keep the day goi
 ng\, we’ll finish with a cozy **Thanksgiving lunch at Swiss Chalet**.\n\
 nTheir seasonal special is expected to be around **$18.29 plus tax and tip
 ** and includes stuffing\, cranberry sauce\, your choice of side\, a roll\
 , and a slice of pie — a pretty good way to finish a Thanksgiving walk! 
 🦃🥧\n\n📱 Don't forget to join our **WhatsApp Group – [CLICK HERE
 ](https://chat.whatsapp.com/H59mSCbsAi018gYANrKAnc)**\n\n***\n\n### Meetup
  Details\n\n📍 **Meetup Location:** I will be standing outside of ST. CL
 AIR SUBWAT STATION right beside the McDonald wearing my Moose Hat. 🦌\n
 🕛 **Meetup Time:** 12:00pm\n**I will only wait 5 minutes.**\n💲 **Mee
 tup Fee:** $5 cash 💵 or e-transfer 📲 to **[mathewmaclean@hotmail.com
 ](mailto:mathewmaclean@hotmail.com)**\n📍 **Ending Spot:** Swiss Chalet\
 , a few blocks from the station.\n\nPlanning to join us for lunch? Please 
 let me know so I can give Swiss Chalet a rough estimate of how many people
  to expect. They don’t take reservations\, but I’d like to give them a
 n approximate number so they can be prepared for our group.\n\n🍁 **Plea
 se note:** Swiss Chalet is a continuation of this event\, not a separate e
 vent for anyone joining us for the walk. If you are attending the Brick Wo
 rks walk **and** joining us for lunch at Swiss Chalet\, you only pay the *
 *$5 Meetup fee once**.\nIf you are **only joining us at Swiss Chalet** and
  are not attending the walk\, please sign up for the separate Swiss Chalet
  event. The **$5 Meetup fee applies** to that event.\n\n***\n\n### What to
  Bring\n\n* Water\n* Good walking shoes 👟\n* A jacket or extra layer 
 — fall weather can change quickly\n* Your camera or phone if you want to
  capture the colours! 📸\n\n***\n\n### More About the Brick Works 🧱\n
 \nFrom 1889 through the 1980s\, the Don Valley Brick Works was one of Cana
 da’s leading brickyards. In the 1990s\, the former quarry was restored b
 y the City of Toronto and the Toronto and Region Conservation Authority\, 
 transforming the site into the natural and cultural destination we know to
 day.\nOpened to the public in 1996\, Evergreen Brick Works now combines hi
 story\, nature\, wildlife\, and trails in the heart of Toronto’s ravine 
 system. In autumn\, the surrounding landscape comes alive with reds\, oran
 ges\, and golds\, making it one of the city's great places to enjoy the fa
 ll colours.\n\n***\n\n✨ **Not sure yet? You can just show up on the day!
 **\n⚠️ **Sometimes things happen and I may need to cancel. Please watc
 h for updates before heading out.**\n\n👤 **Organized by Mathew.**\nFor 
 questions\, post on the Meetup wall or email **[torontomoviesandoutings@ho
 tmail.com](mailto:torontomoviesandoutings@hotmail.com)**
