SUMMARY:The Thanksgiving Pre Dinner Nature Walk and Ice Cream with Friends
 ! 
DESCRIPTION:Try New Things in Toronto!\nHello everyone\,\n\nCome join us t
 his **Thanksgiving** for a fun afternoon of ice cream\, autumn colours\, a
  beautiful nature walk and good company! It’s a chance to get outside\, 
 enjoy the season and spend some time with friends—before we all sit down
  together for a wonderful Thanksgiving dinner.\n\nJoined by my other group
 s too :)\n\nEvent Details below:\n\nHope you can join us!\n\nSincerely\,\n
 \nSteve Flemming\n(Organizer/Host)\n\n**Event Details:**\n**The Thanksgivi
 ng Pre Dinner Nature Walk and Ice Cream with Friends!**\n\nA few things to
  look forward to:\n• A relaxed autumn nature walk\n• Beautiful fall co
 lours and fresh air\n• An icebreaker game to help everyone get acquainte
 d\n• Ice cream early on in the walk\n• Lots of time to chat\, laugh an
 d meet new people\n• A friendly atmosphere where coming on your own is a
 bsolutely welcome\nAnd after our walk\, the day isn’t over! We’ll be e
 njoying a wonderful Thanksgiving turkey dinner with all the Thanksgiving s
 pirit that goes along with it.\n\n**Friendly Reminders:**\n\n\\*Joined by 
 my other social groups too\; so we can anticipate a fabulous turn out with
  lots of friendly peers to enjoy the day!\n\n\\*Please note we are at **Th
 e Pheasant: A Firkin Pub** at 1999 Avenue Road (roughly 6 blocks north of 
 Lawrence - south of the 401 **(we will meet outfront on the patio/or just 
 outside the patio)**\n\n**Event Fee: $5 (Covers the Walk portion of the Ev
 ent and Entrance into the Post Dinner Party)**\nPayment can be made **in c
 ash at the event** or **in advance by e-transfer to Steveflemming11@gmail.
 com**\n\n**When to meet?**\n-Arrive between 3:00 pm and 3:30 pm\n**Parking
  and Transportation:**\n\\*Lots of street parking on avenue and free resid
 ential parking\n[https://www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/](https:/
 /www.firkinpubs.com/thepheasantandfirkin/)\n(15-20 minute walk from Yonge 
 & Lawrence subway station-or simply take bus or uber from the station)
